WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.384 --> 00:00:03.425
Edward ran as fast as possible from the farm.

2
00:00:03.445 --> 00:00:06.046
He didn't dare look back until he reached the nearby woods.

3
00:00:06.066 --> 00:00:07.187
"Phew! That was close!"

4
00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:09.828
Edward was panting, but he had to keep moving.

5
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:32.581
After a while he stopped to listen for footsteps behind him.

6
00:00:33.721 --> 00:00:37.263
But he heard only birds singing in the bare branches above his head.

7
00:00:40.143 --> 00:00:43.504
He shivered as a cold breeze hit his sweat-soaked rags.

8
00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:47.446
"I have to find a safe place to hide."

9
00:00:49.346 --> 00:00:54.828
Edward ran on and on, frantically searching for a cave, an abandoned house, anything.

10
00:00:58.652 --> 00:01:02.514
As gloom settled over the woods, Edward realized that night was coming.

11
00:01:03.655 --> 00:01:07.677
By now it was too dark to see, and he tripped over roots.

12
00:01:10.099 --> 00:01:13.401
A vine brushed his face, and he fell into a briar patch.

13
00:01:15.082 --> 00:01:18.264
At last Edward spotted a light coming from a hut.

14
00:01:20.425 --> 00:01:25.028
He cautiously peered through a window and spotted a man with long, white hair.

15
00:01:26.812 --> 00:01:30.275
Edward decided the man was harmless despite the ax on the wall.

16
00:01:30.295 --> 00:01:36.359
"He's probably a woodsman who likes living alone," Edward thought.

17
00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:42.483
He knocked on the door, and the man called out, "Who's there?"

18
00:01:42.503 --> 00:01:44.624
"King Edward!"

19
00:01:46.626 --> 00:01:49.388
The woodsman opened the door and studied Edward's rags.

20
00:01:49.408 --> 00:01:54.331
"I've turned away many people," he said.

21
00:01:56.224 --> 00:02:02.028
"But I welcome a king who has given up the splendors of royalty.

22
00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:06.992
You will live here in peace forever."

23
00:02:08.973 --> 00:02:17.719
"Actually Edward looked around the simply furnished room that smelled of wood smoke and mold.

24
00:02:17.739 --> 00:02:20.261
"I was just seeking shelter for tonight."

25
00:02:20.281 --> 00:02:24.204
"We'll see about that."

26
00:02:25.396 --> 00:02:27.957
The woodsman beckoned for Edward to sit by the fire.

27
00:02:27.977 --> 00:02:34.440
"I suppose you're wondering why I'm here," Edward said.

28
00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:37.061
"Not really."

29
00:02:38.802 --> 00:02:42.404
And with that, the man launched into a rambling tale about himself.

30
00:02:44.405 --> 00:02:46.506
Edward felt more uneasy by the minute.

31
00:02:48.486 --> 00:02:50.567
"I might have been safer with John and Frank!"

32
00:02:51.048 --> 00:02:51.648
Edward thought.

33
00:02:53.628 --> 00:02:57.792
Finally the woodsman stopped talking and prepared a supper of bread and cheese.

34
00:02:59.333 --> 00:03:02.716
Edward relaxed, thinking, "This won't be so bad."

35
00:03:05.398 --> 00:03:09.081
That night the old man came into the room where Edward was falling asleep.

36
00:03:09.101 --> 00:03:17.368
"If you're King Edward," he said, "then King Henry must be dead."

37
00:03:17.388 --> 00:03:22.292
"Yes," Edward replied in a sleepy voice.

38
00:03:23.976 --> 00:03:30.822
"I only live like this because King Henry stole my house and my land."

39
00:03:31.783 --> 00:03:35.626
The woodsman waited for Edward to reply, but he was already asleep.

40
00:03:38.168 --> 00:03:40.970
The woodsman went into the other room and studied the fire.

41
00:03:42.831 --> 00:03:45.374
He took his ax off the wall and felt the blade.

42
00:03:45.394 --> 00:03:50.498
"Needs sharpening," he muttered, and went to work.

43
00:03:54.148 --> 00:03:56.631
After midnight he crept into Edward's room.

44
00:03:58.052 --> 00:04:00.735
Without a word, he bound and gagged the boy.

45
00:04:03.978 --> 00:04:07.602
The next morning Edward woke up with the woodsman standing over him.

46
00:04:08.924 --> 00:04:11.826
He struggled against the ropes that bound his hands and feet.

47
00:04:11.847 --> 00:04:16.832
"Not so fast," the woodsman said.

48
00:04:18.188 --> 00:04:24.792
"You're not going anywhere until you apologize for your father's cruelty."

49
00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:29.634
"Mmff!" The gag prevented Edward from talking.

50
00:04:30.735 --> 00:04:34.057
His eyes were wild with fear, and his heart was pounding.

51
00:04:35.778 --> 00:04:38.479
Suddenly there was the sound of voices outside the hut.

52
00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:42.461
The woodsman threw a blanket over Edward and left the room.

53
00:04:44.503 --> 00:04:46.744
Edward could hear men fighting and running away.

54
00:04:49.004 --> 00:04:51.245
Then there was a loud knock at the door to the hut.

55
00:04:51.265 --> 00:04:53.827
"Open this door immediately!"

56
00:04:55.047 --> 00:04:55.688
"It's Miles!"

57
00:04:56.068 --> 00:04:57.829
Edward thought, filled with relief.

58
00:04:57.849 --> 00:05:00.770
"Where's the boy?"

59
00:05:01.191 --> 00:05:02.051
Miles demanded.

60
00:05:06.413 --> 00:05:08.454
boy?" the woodsman asked.

61
00:05:09.695 --> 00:05:11.076
"You know who I mean.

62
00:05:11.496 --> 00:05:12.657
King Edward!

63
00:05:13.757 --> 00:05:18.500
I caught the scoundrels who kidnapped him, and they confessed they'd tracked him to your door."

64
00:05:20.396 --> 00:05:21.256
"Come on, Miles!"

65
00:05:21.757 --> 00:05:22.417
Edward thought.

66
00:05:22.437 --> 00:05:25.058
"Stop talking and rescue me!"

67
00:05:25.078 --> 00:05:30.920
"You mean that ragged boy who showed up last night?"

68
00:05:31.381 --> 00:05:32.801
the woodsman said innocently.

69
00:05:32.821 --> 00:05:36.683
"I sent him on an errand."

70
00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:39.644
"An errand?

71
00:05:40.264 --> 00:05:42.025
Wait! What's that noise?"

72
00:05:43.526 --> 00:05:48.288
While the two men talked, Edward had been moaning, trying to attract Miles' attention.

73
00:05:50.752 --> 00:05:55.535
"That sound is just the wind in the trees," the woodsman said.

74
00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:59.078
"Come outside and I'll show you."

75
00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:04.742
Edward groaned in despair as he heard the door shut.

76
00:06:05.762 --> 00:06:09.405
But his spirits improved when the men came back inside a few minutes later.

77
00:06:09.425 --> 00:06:14.268
"I can't wait any longer," Miles said.

78
00:06:14.288 --> 00:06:16.170
"I have to leave.

79
00:06:17.531 --> 00:06:19.232
Edward must have lost his way in the woods."

80
00:06:20.412 --> 00:06:21.833
"Don't go alone.

81
00:06:23.154 --> 00:06:25.575
Let me help you search for him."

82
00:06:28.577 --> 00:06:31.258
As the door closed, Edward lost all hope.

83
00:06:31.278 --> 00:06:36.261
"That old man will get rid of Miles and come back to harm me!"

84
00:06:37.462 --> 00:06:39.242
He soon heard the door open again.

85
00:06:40.563 --> 00:06:43.425
Edward hoped it was Miles, but he was afraid to look.

86
00:06:44.826 --> 00:06:47.447
Instead John and Frank entered the room.

87
00:06:50.324 --> 00:06:52.007
"You're not who I expected!"

88
00:06:52.488 --> 00:06:55.273
Edward said, but he was still happy when they freed him.

89
00:06:56.855 --> 00:07:01.363
Without a word, his old enemies grabbed him by the wrists and hurried him out the door.
